        "Hyde and Knudsen used 23° prisms, then altered vision separately in central and peripheral regions of the visual field. Each manipulation changed one visual region at a time. The resulting auditory adjustments depended on which part of visual space remained available to the animal. The regional result shows that the visual source of each adjustment matters.",
